<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    C# bindings for SDL3.

    WHY THIS IS ITS OWN PROJECT
    ===========================
    The implementation plan (Phase 3 preamble) left this unassigned: "the vendored
    SDL3-CS.cs is introduced by WP-2.1 in an Android context, but desktop needs it
    too. Decide where it lives (new Platform.SDL3 project vs. inside Splash.OpenGL)
    and record it in the WP-2.1 PR."

    Decision: its own project, for three reasons.

      1. Splash.OpenGL is the thing being deleted. Putting SDL3 inside the project
         named after the dependency we are removing means WP-3.x would have to move
         it again, during the single riskiest refactor in the plan.
      2. Consumers are not all renderers. Wuka (Android), Karawan, examples/Launcher,
         Testbed and TestRunner all need windowing; only some of them need Splash.
         A leaf project with no dependencies can be referenced by all of them without
         dragging the renderer along.
      3. It is vendored third-party source, and keeping it isolated keeps
         "do not edit this file" enforceable at a directory boundary rather than by
         convention. See vendor/README.md for provenance and the update procedure.

    NO PackageReference here, deliberately: SDL3-CS ships as source, and the native
    libSDL3.so comes from Karawan.Natives (built by our own pinned CI, WP-1.2/1.3).
    That is the whole point of the migration - one pinned source for the native, one
    pinned source for the binding, and no third party in between.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <!-- SDL3-CS is pointer-based interop throughout. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <!--
      Vendored generated code. We do not own its style, and we do not want its
      warnings drowning ours - but we do NOT silence them repository-wide, only for
      this project, which contains nothing else.
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS0649;CS0169;CS8500;CA1401;SYSLIB1054</NoWarn>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>false</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    vendor/SDL3.Core.cs is picked up by the SDK's default Compile glob; listing it
    explicitly as well is a NETSDK1022 duplicate-item error.
  -->

</Project>
